//RS //! D-CAP-RECEIVER1=D: mark the value, not the call.
//RS //!
//RS //! A `&` or `^` mark sits on the named place a method call writes or takes:
//RS //! `&buf.append(" world")`, `^buf.seal()`, `&items[i].append("!")`. The parser
//RS //! binds the mark to the maximal place (a name plus fields, indexes, or
//RS //! ranges) that the first call of a chain receives. Sema owns the check: the
//RS //! MethodCall arm lifts the mark off the receiver before resolution, every
//RS //! receiver-convention hook records the resolved convention for that
//RS //! receiver, and the arm then compares the written mark with that
//RS //! convention. Resolution, place evaluation, argument order, two-phase
//RS //! borrowing, and move checks see exactly the unmarked call they always saw.
//RS //! A write window receiver (`&values[0..1].sort()`) keeps its `&place`
//RS //! construction (D-SHAPE-PLACE1=A) and is not re-checked here.
//RS 
